  <static seed="175" source="Contrib/DMOI/1-Counting/1_7-Chapter_Summary/1_7_16.pg">
    <statement><p>Suppose you have 19 one-dollar bills to give out as prizes to your top 6 discrete math students. How many ways can you do this if: 
<ol label="a.">
<li>
<p>Each of the 6 students gets at least 1 dollar?</p>
<p><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0001"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Some students might get nothing?</p>
<p><fillin characters="5" name="AnSwEr0002"/></p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Each student gets at least 1 dollar but no more than 8 dollars?</p>
<p><fillin characters="15" name="AnSwEr0003"/></p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</statement>
    <hint><p>Use stars and bars.</p>
</hint>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\mathop{\rm C}\nolimits\mathopen{}\left(18,13\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>\mathop{\rm C}\nolimits\mathopen{}\left(24,19\right)</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>8568-1512</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><p><ol label="a.">
<li>
<p><m>{18 \choose 13}={8568}</m> ways.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{24 \choose 19}={42504}</m> ways.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>{18 \choose 13} - \left[{6 \choose 1}{11 \choose 5} - {6 \choose 2}{4 \choose 5} \dots \right]={7056}</m> ways.</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</solution>
